## Status
E1 is a **development set**: the race criterion's capture rule (capture only while p >= p_-) was fixed after seeing quick runs, so E1 is not pre-registered.
E1b is the **held-out confirmatory** test: `results/e1b/prediction.json` was committed (0576788) before its runs. Disclosed there: 6 grid cells (seed 0) were run as a sanity check before the pre-registration was written; no predictor logic changed afterwards except an overflow rescaling in `n1_general`. After the pre-registration, the run script gained only measurement-side robustness: a run whose Euler iteration blows up is stopped and recorded as `diverged` instead of crashing the sweep (the first launch crashed on such a run).
E1c is a second held-out test, of the one post-hoc correction made after E1b (the depth-L capture nullcline, motivated by E1b's depth failure): `results/e1c/prediction.json` was committed (b84e38e) before any E1c run; no E1c code changed between that commit and the runs.
E2 has `results/e2/prediction.json` committed (db2a53b) before any E2 run. E3 has `results/e3/prediction.json` committed before any sweep run (the commit that adds it; the step-0 init job only evaluates the untrained networks). The E3 run scripts record that commit in each run's `provenance.json`.


## E3 headline (pre-registered; from `results/e3/summary.json`, `summary_followup.json`)
- **Is E3 in the theory's regime? Only partly; it is a transfer test.** Arm T meets the assumptions on the optimiser and target (SGD with momentum, stop-gradient copy target, decay on every parameter, no predictor LayerNorm). It does not meet these: a linear encoder and predictor (here a 4-block ViT with a 3-block transformer predictor), a start near collapse (standard init, gain 1; at gain 0.1 nothing moved in the pilot), population gradients, and co-diagonal statistics. Arm P (AdamW I-JEPA recipe, LayerNorms, EMA schedule) is further outside.
- **C-rank: Arm T PASS, Arm P FAIL.** Spearman between the step-0 horizon-rule count and the epoch-20 count: Arm T rho 0.83, 95% CI [0.45, 0.99] (12 configs); Arm P 0.12 [-0.32, 0.47] (20 configs). In Arm T this rests on the weight-decay sweep (post hoc split, `summary.json` `post_hoc`, not registered): Spearman 1.0 over the 6 wd configs (count 51, 39, 24, 8.7, 5, 4 for wd 0 ... 0.1, predicted 55, 36, 30, 18, 7, 2) and 0.27 [-0.58, 1.0] over the other 6, five of which share the baseline prediction 18. The rule misses predictor init badly: T_pinit3 is predicted 115 and measured 10.3.
- **C-loc (critical weight decay, Arm T): FAIL.** The observed transition is at 0.0055 (between 0.003, healthy, and 0.01, collapsed) against the predicted 0.014: a factor 2.6, outside the registered factor 2. The rule puts the transition too late.
- **C-dir: signed pairs 5 of 6 hold, nulls 7 of 20 hold.**
  - Signed: Arm T wd (3 of 3), P depth 3 -> 6 and T pred-init 1 -> 3 hold; P pred-init 1 -> 3 fails. T pred-init holds in sign only: RankMe 8.6 -> 9.2, against a predicted count of 18 -> 115.
